W44-RECON-DEEP/A9 — bit-identical diffmap divergence test
==========================================================
Date     : 2026-05-23
Workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-recon-deep-a9
Branch   : main (no source change; harness + script only)
Harness  : jxl-encoder/examples/w44_recon_deep_a9_diffmap_dump.rs
Runner   : scripts/w44_recon_deep_a9/run_pairs.sh
Analyzer : scripts/w44_recon_deep_a9/analyze_pfm_pair.py

Inputs   : 6 (reference, distorted) PNG pairs, all metadata-stripped
           via `convert -strip` so libjxl + Rust crate load identical
           pixel bytes through identical sRGB->linear paths.
           - identity_terminal       : terminal.png vs itself (smoke)
           - identity_1418519        : 1418519.png vs itself (smoke)
           - synthetic_gradient_512  : 512x512 horizontal gradient vs
                                       gaussian-blur(sigma=1.0) of same
           - photo_1418519_d5        : 1418519 vs cjxl-encoded-djxl-decoded d=5
           - screen_terminal_d4      : terminal vs cjxl-encoded-djxl-decoded d=4
           - photo_1418519_d10       : 1418519 vs cjxl-encoded-djxl-decoded d=10

Per-cell tools:
  - libjxl: ~/work/jxl-efforts/libjxl/build/tools/butteraugli_main
           with --rawdistmap <out.pfm>  (PFM single-channel Pf, bottom-up)
  - ours  : local butteraugli crate (workspace-patched, ~/work/butteraugli)
           via butteraugli(img1, img2, ButteraugliParams::default()
                          .with_hf_asymmetry(1.0)  // matches libjxl
                          .with_xmul(1.0)          // matches libjxl
                          .with_intensity_target(80.0)  // matches libjxl
                          .with_compute_diffmap(true))

Both sides use identical params (defaults of butteraugli_main.cc:100-110).

Per-cell results (TSV col headers: cell, w, h, libjxl_score, ours_score,
score_rel_diff_pct, diffmap_max_abs, diffmap_p99, diffmap_median,
diffmap_max_rel_pct, argmax_x, argmax_y, note):

| cell                    | w x h        | libjxl_score | ours_score | rel%    | max_abs   | p99       | median    | verdict       |
