| photo_1418519_d5        | 512 x 512    | 4.697474     | 4.697464   | 0.0002  | 1.62e-4   | 5.11e-5   | 6.08e-6   | AT-PARITY     |
| screen_terminal_d4      | 1646 x 1062  | 2.216007     | 2.216006   | 0.0000  | 4.27e-4   | 1.90e-4   | 2.37e-5   | AT-PARITY     |
| photo_1418519_d10       | 512 x 512    | 9.190868     | 9.190875   | 0.0001  | 1.82e-4   | 5.61e-5   | 6.68e-6   | AT-PARITY     |

VERDICT: on real-world photo + screen encode-decode roundtrips, the diffmap
kernel is AT PARITY with libjxl to ~1e-4 max-abs (float-precision noise).
The W44-105 23x scalar score gap (ours=2.07 vs libjxl=47.7 on identical
initial qf) cannot be explained by the diffmap kernel itself.  Its root
cause is upstream — recon-pixel input divergence (matching the W44-138
EPF-stage finding) or sRGB->linear conversion divergence between the
buttloop's ButteraugliReference and our recon-pixel feed.

The synthetic-gradient + blur pair (615% relative score) reproduces the
documented PARITY_PLAN.md known failure: Rust butteraugli systematically
under-scores blur patterns by 20-32% on synthetic test images.  This is a
real crate-level kernel issue but it does NOT match the W44-105 forensic
pattern (W44-105 is on a photo cell, where this test shows the kernel at
parity).  The PARITY_PLAN Phase 2 root causes (Malta filter scaling, mask
blur boundary handling) target this same synthetic-blur cluster.

DO NOT (binding for future agents):
  - DO NOT cite the synthetic-gradient blur divergence as the W44-105
    root cause.  The W44-105 cell is a photo, and on photos the kernel
    is at parity to 1e-4 max-abs (5 orders of magnitude below the 23x
    score gap).
  - DO NOT respawn another "compare diffmap kernels" chunk.  This test
    is conclusive on the real-photo path.
  - DO NOT cite FMA precision for the 1e-4 max-abs delta (per W44-66
    user correction).  The delta is at the magnitude where two
    independent SIMD float reductions land naturally on the same input.

Follow-on candidates:
  1. W44-RECON-DEEP/A10 (recommended next): dump the actual buttloop-
     internal recon pixels (after our reconstruct_xyb + xyb_to_linear_
     rgb_planar) AND libjxl's RoundtripImage output on the same cell
     (initial qf, iter 0).  Compare per-pixel.  If max-abs > 1e-3 on
     RGB channels in linear space, that IS the W44-105 root cause and
     P-1 (per-iter sharpness recompute) is the right fix.  If max-abs
     < 1e-3, the divergence is in the ButteraugliReference vs
     SetLinearReferenceImage path (cell-internal sRGB->linear
     mismatch).
  2. PARITY_PLAN.md Phase 1-2 work for synthetic blur.  Lower priority
     than A10 because (a) the blur failure mode is on synthetic content
     not in any production cell, and (b) the ~20-32% kernel-level under-
     scoring on blur does NOT scale up to the 23x W44-105 gap.

